  "task": "X52 h=4 centered field-uniformity",
  "theorem": "Let F be any field of odd characteristic and H <= F^* be cyclic of even order n. For s != 0, unordered H-pairs with sum s are in two-to-one correspondence with ratios r in H\\{1} satisfying 1+r in sH.  Hence shell sizes are constant on F^*/H-cosets.  If F is finite, the n-th power map has kernel H, so the quotient coset can be represented by s^n.  X49's quotient energy and X50's threshold are therefore field-uniform, not prime-field artifacts."
